# Denylist, not an allowlist.  Rewritten Sep 14, 2026.
#
# This file used to open with a bare `*` and then re-admit ~110 paths one at a
# time.  That inverted arrangement broke the same way five separate times, and
# always silently: a new file or directory simply never got committed, the
# deploy looked fine, and the missing asset surfaced later as a 404.  The trap
# has a second edge — git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so
# `!assets/downloads/` did nothing until `!assets/` un-ignored the parent.
# Nobody can be expected to remember that at 1am.
#
# So: ignore the handful of things that genuinely must not be committed, and
# track everything else by default.  A new page, card, script or asset is now
# committed because it exists, not because someone remembered to add a line.
#
# NOTE: this governs what is TRACKED.  What is SERVED publicly is governed
# separately by .assetsignore — ops docs are committed but never published.

# ---- secrets: never, under any circumstances ----
itn-secrets.env
itn-git-credential.sh
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# ---- private, must never reach the public site ----
# The pick ledger is the only record of real performance and is deliberately
# not public.  Keeping it out of git keeps it off the deploy entirely.
PICK_LEDGER.md

# ---- build artifacts regenerated every run ----
issue.json

# ---- local noise ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
*.log
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
